WEBVTT

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.410
Line's busy.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:56.940
Who's on the phone
at a time like this?

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.720
Hey! Who're you talking to?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.740
Ikuko.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:09.960
What?!

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:11.930
Give me the phone!

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.030
Hello? Ikuko?

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:15.960
May I speak to your grandpa?

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.640
What?

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.800
What?

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.870
Ten more yen.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.080
There's no need for that.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:27.150
As a trustee of
a school board...

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.210
Mr. Otonashi is on
a trip to Hong Kong.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.460
Huh?

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.280
When's he comin' back?

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.730
Day after tomorrow,
in the morning.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.020
What?

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:44.020
Ikuko hasn't heard anything
about tearing down Maison Ikkoku.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.580
Anyway, until my
father-in-law comes back--

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.830
What? We just wait and see?

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:14.990
Well--

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.400
Whatcha gonna do if,
as soon as he comes home...

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.050
he says, "Oh, yeah.
That's right"?

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:26.550
I'm disappointed. I never thought
our landlord would do such a thing.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.700
That may not be the case.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.520
That's right! Even Ikuko's
parents know nothing about it.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.550
Maybe the old man's
acting on his own.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.680
He wouldn't.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.580
How can you be so calm?

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:44.800
The one who's gonna lose out most if
Maison Ikkoku should disappear, is YOU.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.460
Me?

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:51.330
Maison Ikkoku is the ONLY LINK
you have to the manager!

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.580
Let's all try to find out
the source of this rumor.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.480
Great idea!

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.360
Fine.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.740
That's all we can do.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.480
I'll ask our real estate
agent about it.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.110
Mitsukoshi.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.900
You help us, too, okay?

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.040
I'm sorry you just moved in,
and this happens.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.830
Please. I'm sure this is
a bigger concern to you.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.330
So let's drink up!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.810
Yeah!

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:35.600
Let's!

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.540
What are you all thinking
at a time like this?

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.380
Loosen up, man!

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:05.400
The real estate agent never
heard about a demolition.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:09.210
But he did say something
that bothered me.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.670
What?

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.380
You know that apartment
building up the slope...

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.510
that's sort of
like our place?

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:23.920
Its landlord passed away last year,
and his son inherited it.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.650
And the son wanted
to demolish the building...

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.520
and build a bigger complex.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.670
So someone mistook that story
for Maison Ikkoku, huh?

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.000
That's strange.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.150
According to my sources...

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.080
it was definitely Maison Ikkoku
that was rumored to be demolished.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.510
Who didja hear that from?

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.670
My co-workers.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.390
Where at?!

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.820
That's a SECRET!

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:54.350
But my sources are reliable.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.830
Even among my customers,

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.920
no one ever mentioned a building
other than Maison Ikkoku.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.590
What the hell's goin' on?

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.910
You again?

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.580
Hi again.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:34.570
Wanna talk?

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.220
Here you go.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.530
The rumor about the demolition?

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:52.650
I overheard people at the
gas station talking about it.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.650
Did they clearly
mention "Maison Ikkoku"?

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.980
Yeah. They were talking about...

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.960
how Maison Ikkoku's property
would be worth such and such.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:03.900
I see.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.650
So is the rumor true?

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.290
We don't know yet.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.770
We have no way of
verifying it right now.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.520
H-How about the other rumor?

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:16.900
Ms. Oto--

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.600
That Ms. Otonashi's remarying!

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.380
Oh, that.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.950
That's a complete lie...

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.560
is what I wish
I could say, but...

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:33.520
So it's true?

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.280
No. I don't think so.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:38.460
But...

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.210
See you later.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.440
Oh! Welcome back.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.040
Hello.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.980
Mr. Mitsukoshi gave
this melon to all of us.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.120
He said his client
gave it to him.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.400
Client?

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.650
Uh-huh. Let's all have it later.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.510
Hello?

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.270
Hi, Kozue.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:44.630
Have you ever
heard of "M.H.T."?

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:46.920
What's that?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.760
It's a real estate company
called My Home Town.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:51.550
And?

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.980
Well, I've been seeing
that Mr. Mitsukoshi...

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.850
go in and out of their
Shinjuku office all the time.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.880
How did you know?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:04.470
It's on my way home
from school... that office.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:12.440
I just remembered something.
I gotta go.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.020
Godai!

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.060
What are you doing?

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:05.110
That man that you
passed at the door--

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:07.300
That was Mitsukoshi.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:08.380
What?

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.670
Mitaka! Let's go!

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.650
A-All right!

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:29.260
So Kozue was right.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:30.290
Uh-huh.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.730
So what did they say
at the office?

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:36.240
It seemed suspicious, all right.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.170
As soon as I mentioned
Clock Tower Hill...

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.850
I sensed tension in the air.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.310
I see.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.540
So Mitsukoshi is
a spy from MHT?

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:48.720
Yeah.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.520
Let's go confront them.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:53.820
What?

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.490
We know Mitsukoshi's
there right now.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:00.090
I think you should
hold off on that.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.100
We need to tell
Ms. Otonashi first.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.470
Do you think so?

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:05.730
Yes.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:09.800
If she's being deceived,
then she needs to know.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:32.740
That can't be!

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.990
Are you telling me...

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.440
that Mr. Mitsukoshi works
for that company...

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.870
and is spreading those rumors?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:46.780
We don't know for sure, but
don't you think something's fishy?

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.250
Mr. Mitsukoshi would
never do such a thing!

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:56.240
He's not the kind of person
who would betray others.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.750
But he clearly has something
to do with that company.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:01.120
I'm sure he has his reasons.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.940
We could be totally mistaken.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:12.160
I understand your take on this.
Let me ask him about it myself.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.720
Don't worry. I'm a manager.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.240
I can see through lies.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.610
All right.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:24.190
So until I do, please don't
say anything to the others.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.560
Kentaro! Dinner's ready!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:58.990
'Kay!

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:00.320
See ya.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:00.910
Yup.

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:05.860
Big Brother Godai!

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.260
That's just a rumor, right?

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:14.630
Of course. Ikuko's grandpa would
never do such a horrible thing.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.110
Yup!

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.100
Ma! Let's eat!

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.860
I wish I could
believe my own words.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:30.080
Yotsuya!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.490
Were you expecting
a tofu delivery man?

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:35.090
NO!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.370
He's late...

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:11.610
Godai! I thought you
were goin' to the toilet!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:13.020
I'll be right there.

00:14:13.340 --> 00:14:15.600
Don't use our
first floor bathroom.

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.260
You'll use up our toilet paper!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.620
Geez!

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:29.810
Hello!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.010
Hi.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.460
It looks like rain.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:36.710
Yes.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.510
Aren't you going? Upstairs?

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:42.880
Huh? Yes. I'll be going.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.560
This is for you all.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.100
Octopus puffs.

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.150
T-Thanks.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:52.020
Oh, welcome home.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:53.620
Hello.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:57.230
Um... I need to speak to you.

00:14:57.350 --> 00:14:57.970
Sure.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.820
I-I'll take this to the gang.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:19.990
I see. Caught in the act.

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:24.440
Yes. I wanted to
get this cleared up.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.110
Otherwise, you'll feel
uncomfortable here.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.360
I see.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.950
It's true I've been
frequenting that office.

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.680
But as a client.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:42.280
To tell you the truth,
I was born there.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.960
In the olden days, that area
was lined with tenement housing.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:51.430
A local train line ran
in front of my house.

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.390
There's no trace of it now.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.900
When I think of my home...

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:59.600
that used to stand where
that building is now...

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.130
it brings back memories.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.330
Do you believe me?

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:31.790
Thank you very much.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:32.960
Oh... Please.

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:36.340
Please stay as
long as you want.

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:37.530
Yes.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:43.500
What a great place this is.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.910
It's a really great place.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:49.140
Yes.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:03.030
No way! That sounds
too convenIent!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.290
But I don't think he was lying.

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.680
I'll ask him myself!

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:10.150
Hey!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.680
What'cha two doin' here?

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:14.120
Godai! No fair!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.640
Come here and party!

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.840
I have to talk
to Mitsukoshi about--

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.570
NO!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.950
Where is he, anyway?

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:24.680
Mitsukoshi! You're gonna
miss out on the octopus puffs!

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:28.130
Mrs. Ichinose, Mr. Mitsukoshi
went to the bath house.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.490
Oh. Let's start without him.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.220
Next morning, a telegram
arrived for Mitsukoshi

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:56.810
From an unidentified sender.

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:59.920
It read: "report to
the office immediately."

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:03.080
Mitsukoshi!

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:05.730
Are you in there?

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.400
There's a telegram for you!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.030
Do you hear anything?

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:10.700
Not at all.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.670
I don't see anything from the window.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.170
Let's open his door.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.210
Y-Yes.

00:18:34.970 --> 00:18:36.930
A barrel of sake.

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.520
How cool.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.870
So that demolition rumor is--

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.030
Of course it's not true!

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:56.310
I would never think
of doing that...

00:18:56.390 --> 00:18:57.840
without consulting
you first, Kyoko!

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:00.810
Why would such a rumor spread?

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.720
I was surprised when
I heard it from Ikuko.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:06.460
In any case,
as long as I'm around...

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:09.060
I'd never tear down
Maison Ikkoku!

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:41.970
So he was a spy
from that company!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.020
No, he wasn't an employee
of that company.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.590
He was one of those agents
contracted to seek out ideal locations

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:50.640
on which to build
new residential buildings.

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:54.940
He looked like he
couldn't even hurt a fly.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.070
Yeah. I could see Yotsuya
doin' that sorta thing.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.710
I only do things
that make people happy.

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:02.300
Whatever.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.620
You know, Manager,
from now on...

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:08.550
you have to be more careful
about the tenants you accept.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:15.280
We were so nice to him
and look what happened.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:16.960
Was he so bad?

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:24.210
Maybe he came to do his job,
but I'm sure he had his reasons.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:28.590
Besides, there was no harm done.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.640
That's what's so strange.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.140
Strange?

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:37.100
Apparently, that company
received a call from Mitsukoshi.

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:42.440
They told me he hung up
after saying "I'm pulling out."

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.810
Pulling out?
From Maison Ikkoku?

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:49.660
They were livid... those
people at that company.

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:52.760
So that telegram...

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.410
He can't go back there...
to that company.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:12.080
When something new is born...

00:21:13.930 --> 00:21:15.890
something old disappears.

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:20.420
That may be inevitable...

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:26.350
but we should not forget
what has disappeared.

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.940
What brings this up?

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:33.030
That's what Mitsukoshi said.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.540
That's what he said to me.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.440
Really?

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:40.690
Yes, at a nearby park.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:43.680
Mitsukoshi said that, huh?

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:05.870
That sake looked
awfully good.

00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:07.830
Shall we drink it?

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.500
Sounds great.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.300
We can, can't we, Manager?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.270
S-Sure.

00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:13.840
Yay!

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:16.270
Godai, we're goin' to your place.

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:19.990
Two nights in a row!

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:22.420
Ma! What about dinner?!

00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:24.250
Make yourself some
instant noodles!

00:22:27.470 --> 00:22:28.790
Aren't you going?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:30.870
No.

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.900
He seemed like a nice man
that Mr. Mitsukoshi.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:41.790
Yes. We have lots
of nice people here.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:44.490
Whaddaya doin'?
We're waitin'!

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:47.240
Get your butts up here!
You snooze you lose!

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:49.740
Hey! Don't drink it all! Yotsuya!

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:51.620
That's my sake!

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:53.450
I enjoyed it!

00:22:53.820 --> 00:22:55.380
It wasn't yours!

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:58.620
Are those "nice" people?

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:04.690
I want to drink, too.

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:07.870
Will you join us, Mitaka?

00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:11.440
Why not?
How about you, Ms. Otonashi?

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:13.530
Sure. Go ahead.

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:15.300
I have to take care of the fire.

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:16.940
Okay.

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:18.020
Let's go.

00:23:49.880 --> 00:23:52.310
Four years?
How time flies.

00:23:52.470 --> 00:23:55.490
Forget Soichiro? Never!

00:23:55.880 --> 00:24:00.110
Next: "Forgive me, Soichiro!
Kyoko's Painful Decision to Marry Again!"

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:06.730
Spring breeze blows, petals fly
Awaken from a dream
And my heart still soars
